## 2. DNS Fundamentals

### DNS Hierarchy

```
Root Domain
    ↓
.com TLD (Top Level Domain)
    ↓
example.com (Domain)
    ↓
www.example.com (Subdomain)
api.example.com (Subdomain)
```

### DNS Resolution Process

```
1. User Browser (Recursive Query)
   "What's the IP for example.com?"
    ↓
2. Local Resolver (ISP DNS)
   "Let me ask the Root Nameserver"
    ↓
3. Root Nameserver
   "Ask the .com TLD server"
    ↓
4. .com TLD Nameserver
   "Ask Route 53 (authoritative)"
    ↓
5. Route 53 (Authoritative)
   "The IP is 203.0.113.42"
    ↓
6. Response travels back to browser
    ↓
7. Browser connects to 203.0.113.42
```

### DNS Record Components

```
Name:      example.com
Type:      A (IPv4 address)
Value:     203.0.113.42
TTL:       300 seconds
Routing:   Simple
```

