## 4. Record Types

### Common DNS Record Types

#### A Record (IPv4 Address)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "example.com",
        "Type": "A",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [{"Value": "203.0.113.42"}]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Result: example.com → 203.0.113.42
```

#### AAAA Record (IPv6 Address)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "example.com",
        "Type": "AAAA",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [{"Value": "2001:0db8:85a3:0000:0000:8a2e:0370:7334"}]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Result: example.com → IPv6 address (for modern clients)
```

#### CNAME Record (Canonical Name)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "www.example.com",
        "Type": "CNAME",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [{"Value": "example.com"}]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Result: www.example.com → example.com → IP
# Note: CNAME creates a redirect, adds extra lookup
```

#### MX Record (Mail Exchange)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "example.com",
        "Type": "MX",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [
          {"Value": "10 mail1.example.com"},
          {"Value": "20 mail2.example.com"}
        ]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Result: Emails for example.com go to mail1 (priority 10)
```

#### NS Record (Nameserver)

```bash
# NS records point to nameservers for zone delegation
# Automatically created by Route 53

aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "api.example.com",
        "Type": "NS",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [
          {"Value": "ns1.api.example.com"},
          {"Value": "ns2.api.example.com"}
        ]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Delegates api.example.com to separate nameservers
```

#### TXT Record (Text)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "example.com",
        "Type": "TXT",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [
          {"Value": "\"v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all\""},
          {"Value": "\"google-site-verification=xxxxx\""}
        ]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Used for SPF, DKIM, domain verification
```

#### SOA Record (Start of Authority)

```bash
# Automatically created by Route 53
# Contains zone information:
# - Primary nameserver
# - Admin email
# - Serial number
# - Refresh interval
# - Retry interval
# - Expiration time
# - TTL for negative caching
```

#### SRV Record (Service)

```bash
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "_sip._tcp.example.com",
        "Type": "SRV",
        "TTL": 300,
        "ResourceRecords": [
          {"Value": "10 60 5060 sipserver.example.com"}
        ]
      }
    }]
  }'

# Priority Service Port Target
# 10       60    5060  sipserver.example.com
```

#### ALIAS Record (AWS-specific)

```bash
# ALIAS records are AWS-specific and resolve within AWS
aws route53 change-resource-record-sets \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --change-batch '{
    "Changes": [{
      "Action": "CREATE",
      "ResourceRecordSet": {
        "Name": "example.com",
        "Type": "A",
        "AliasTarget": {
          "HostedZoneId": "Z2FDTNDATAQYW2",
          "DNSName": "d123.cloudfront.net",
          "EvaluateTargetHealth": true
        }
      }
    }]
  }'

# Maps example.com to CloudFront distribution (no TTL needed)
# Automatically updates when CloudFront changes
```

