## 6. Health Checks

### Create Health Check

```bash
# HTTP Health Check
HEALTH_CHECK=$(aws route53 create-health-check \
  --health-check-config \
    IPAddress=203.0.113.42 \
    Port=80 \
    Type=HTTP \
    ResourcePath=/health \
    RequestInterval=30 \
    FailureThreshold=3 \
  --query 'HealthCheck.Id' \
  --output text)

echo "Health Check ID: $HEALTH_CHECK"

# Parameters:
# - IPAddress: Server to check
# - Port: Port to check
# - Type: HTTP, HTTPS, TCP, CALCULATED, CLOUDWATCH
# - ResourcePath: Path to check (/health)
# - RequestInterval: 30 or 10 seconds (fast)
# - FailureThreshold: Mark unhealthy after N failures
```

### Health Check Types

```bash
# HTTPS Health Check
aws route53 create-health-check \
  --health-check-config \
    IPAddress=203.0.113.42 \
    Port=443 \
    Type=HTTPS \
    ResourcePath=/health \
    FullyQualifiedDomainName=example.com \
    SearchString="healthy" \
    RequestInterval=30 \
    FailureThreshold=3

# TCP Health Check (no HTTP)
aws route53 create-health-check \
  --health-check-config \
    IPAddress=203.0.113.42 \
    Port=3306 \
    Type=TCP \
    RequestInterval=30 \
    FailureThreshold=3

# CloudWatch Alarm Health Check
aws route53 create-health-check \
  --health-check-config \
    AlarmIdentifier=arn:aws:cloudwatch:us-east-1:123456789012:alarm:ServerDown

# Calculated Health Check (combination)
aws route53 create-health-check \
  --health-check-config \
    Type=CALCULATED \
    ChildHealthChecks=[health-check-1,health-check-2,health-check-3] \
    HealthThreshold=2
```

### Health Check Flow

```
Every 30 seconds:
1. Route 53 sends HTTP GET /health
2. Server responds with status code
3. Response parsed:
   - 200-299: Healthy ✓
   - Other codes: Unhealthy ✗
   
After 3 failures (90 seconds):
- Mark endpoint as unhealthy
- Stop routing traffic
- Alert via SNS if configured

When healthy again:
- Route 53 retries
- After 1 success: Mark healthy
- Resume routing traffic
```

### Enable Health Check Alerts

```bash
# Create SNS topic for alerts
SNS_TOPIC=$(aws sns create-topic \
  --name route53-health-alerts \
  --query 'TopicArn' \
  --output text)

# Update health check with alarm
aws route53 update-health-check \
  --health-check-id $HEALTH_CHECK \
  --alarm-identifier Name=ServerDown,Region=us-east-1 \
  --insufficient-data-health-status Unhealthy
```

