## 7. Traffic Flow

Traffic Flow enables visual creation of complex routing policies without manual configuration.

### Simple Traffic Flow

```bash
# Create traffic policy
POLICY=$(aws route53 create-traffic-policy \
  --name api-routing \
  --document '{
    "AWSPolicyFormatVersion": "2015-10-01",
    "RecordType": "A",
    "Endpoints": {
      "api-server-1": {
        "Type": "A",
        "IPAddress": "203.0.113.1"
      },
      "api-server-2": {
        "Type": "A",
        "IPAddress": "203.0.113.2"
      }
    },
    "Rules": {
      "rule-1": {
        "RuleType": "failover",
        "Primary": "api-server-1",
        "Secondary": "api-server-2"
      }
    }
  }' \
  --query 'TrafficPolicy.Id' \
  --output text)

# Create traffic policy instance
aws route53 create-traffic-policy-instance \
  --hosted-zone-id $ZONE_ID \
  --name example.com \
  --traffic-policy-id $POLICY \
  --traffic-policy-version 1 \
  --ttl 60
```

