**5. Optimization Techniques**

```
Technique 1: Use ALIAS for AWS Resources

❌ CNAME (extra lookup):
api.example.com CNAME → alb-123.elb.amazonaws.com
app.example.com CNAME → alb-456.elb.amazonaws.com

✓ ALIAS (direct):
api.example.com ALIAS → ALB (resolves automatically)
app.example.com ALIAS → ALB (resolves automatically)

Benefit: No extra DNS queries, faster resolution

Technique 2: Minimize Record Changes
- Avoid changing records frequently
- Plan IP changes in advance
- Batch updates (update multiple records at once)
- Reduces operational overhead

Technique 3: Implement Client-Side Caching
- Browser caches: TTL 300s
- Application caches: TTL 300s
- OS resolver caches: TTL 60-300s
- Result: 90%+ of requests served from cache

Technique 4: Query Logging (Optional)
- Can track all 100k QPS queries
- Useful for debugging
- Adds CloudWatch cost ($5-10/month)
- Only enable if needed for troubleshooting
```

